    {
      "id": "1549959007249108994",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-17T01:43:44.174+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "The stepper drives a screw that pushes up the pins. The pusher part is just an insert that slides down inside. \nGiven the timeframe, I have to choose what is most likely to work, even though you can see it still took a number of revisions (I don't even think that was all)\nIn the end, the number of pins had to be reduced (kept getting 'bed of nails' effect) and the vacuum needed to be embedded in the tip with some internal chambers as I was having a hard time getting seals any other way. \nAs I've understood the design requirements more, I think I would try for some voice coil/solenoid options for the pins and that would allow for smaller space and fidelity on the for pin selection? That's the idea, but need to move to other areas now. \n\n*re: *odrive, I don't think it's not really necessary for what we have at the moment as simplicity is desired.",
      "author": {
        "id": "756011607603019777",
        "name": "anfroholic",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Andrew Wingate",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [
          {
