    {
      "id": "1549971520317685793",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-17T02:33:27.522+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "If you think there's practical potential to modify this very design a little and add load cells into the structural backing of those pins (ideally individually) wired out to something that could eventually record and collate to what the machine was tasked with to mostly-passively gather information about the forces actually involved in the pushing work.....\n\nWhile ofc not matching individual linear motor actuation of any particular variety (there's a reason \"limited slip\" differentials are a thing for 4WD cars....), it'd still give understanding of the forces involved and thus what nuanced actuation in the future would need force-wise/power-wise.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
