      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "well, the operating principle of odrive can give you a lot of speed for the seek while letting you control the deceleration good enough to keep the mechanics from ringing (much) and then still using the encoder resolution to do the fine positioning.\n\nIf you buy from them it's somewhat more expensive than steppers but you do get more speed offered and substantially higher efficciency.\nThough ofc regenerative braking doesn't matter as much for this as it does for a battery powered robot.",
