    {
      "id": "1549975511210533037",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-17T02:49:19.025+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "(I think there'd ideally be a magnetic tube of similar cross section or slightly above compared to the inner rod's magnetic iron part, around the outside of the windings, acting as shielding and to channel the magnetic field where it's wanted.\nBut switched reluctance motors like those technically would be are vulnerable to kinda-non-intuitive design-effects/behaviors, hence kinda preferring to sim. Thankfully the almost trivial geometry involved would make this part of the design almost trivial to pull off.)",
      "author": {
